# supaschema migration policy (Codex rules surface).
# Enforcement: write-time denial of hand-edits to generated migrations is
# owned by .codex/hooks/supaschema-tool-gate.mjs (PreToolUse), and automatic
# diff+check on a schema-tree write is owned by
# .codex/hooks/auto-diff-on-schema-change.mjs (PostToolUse). This file
# carries the policy text for review and prompting.
#
# - Consumer setup is one package install. The installed config, schema and
#   migration directories, rule files, skill files, hook scripts, hook wiring,
#   and tagged AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md addendum are part of the package surface.
#   `supaschema init` is a recovery/recreate command, not a required second
#   setup step.
# - If .supaschema/install.json records "pathConfirmationNeeded": true,
#   inspect the detected candidates, ask the user which schemaPaths and
#   migrationsDir to use, and update supaschema.config.json before the first
#   diff. Do not generate from the installer's guessed first candidate; the
#   PostToolUse hook must skip auto-diff until confirmation is resolved.
# - supaschema.config.json owns adapter, schemaPaths, migrationsDir, typesFile,
#   zodFile, managedSchemas, transactionMode, and named environments. adapter
#   "auto" is the default automated supaschema workflow for generating
#   migrations, checking/verifying them, and refreshing existing type outputs;
#   it is not a Supabase switch. Provider-specific behavior is expressed through
#   paths, managed schemas, transaction mode, excluded grant roles, and explicit
#   verify flags.
# - Schema intent changes only in the configured declarative SQL tree
#   (schemaPaths in supaschema.config.json), such as database/schemas,
#   supabase/schemas, neon/schemas, aws-postgresql/schemas, cloud-sql/schemas,
#   alloydb/schemas, or azure-postgresql/schemas. Render migrations with
#   `supaschema diff`, never hand-author SQL the tree can express.
# - SQL understanding is AST/model-owned. Classify, compare, or mutate DDL
#   through PostgreSQL parse trees (libpg-query) and structured model helpers,
#   not ad hoc regex. Regex is acceptable for outer transport concerns such as
#   hook patch headers, file markers, or redaction, not SQL semantics.
# - A .sql file containing the `-- supaschema: lineage` marker is a generated
#   artifact: change the tree and regenerate; never hand-edit it. The
#   PreToolUse hook blocks direct edits, patch updates, move-target rewrites,
#   and delete/add rewrites. Deleting a stale generated migration is allowed
#   only as deliberate recovery before regenerating from the tree.
# - When the PostToolUse auto-diff hook is wired, writing a schema-tree .sql
#   file auto-runs `supaschema diff` then `supaschema check` and returns the
#   generated migration name or the blocking SUPA_* code as context; treat that
#   as the diff result, resolve any reported code, and do not re-run diff to
#   confirm a clean result. The hook never applies to a database, and it skips
#   multi-root or path-confirmation cases that require human review.
# - Migration writes are no-clobber, and the lineage chain gate must not be
#   bypassed with --no-check-chain without explicit human approval.
# - Destructive changes (drops, column type changes, incompatible view or
#   routine replacements) require the exact object key in hints.destructive
#   after reviewing the rendered SQL; never commit "*".
# - Run `supaschema check` on every migration; run `supaschema verify` before
#   merge when a database is reachable. Keep transactionMode per-migration
#   for transactional runners such as `supabase db push`. CREATE INDEX
#   CONCURRENTLY is blocked in per-migration mode; per-statement lanes produce
#   an explicit .concurrent.sql companion for out-of-transaction review.
# - `supaschema sync` is an explicit operational handoff. With no apply flag it
#   is a dry run; with --local or --remote it gates status and replay safety,
#   then delegates apply/deploy to the Supabase CLI. Do not use apply flags
#   without an explicit human request.
# - Database URLs resolve flag ($ENV indirection supported) > named
#   config.environments entry via --env > SUPASCHEMA_DATABASE_URL > the nearest
#   supabase/config.toml; do not hard-code connection strings.
# - Decode any SUPA_* diagnostic with `supaschema explain <CODE>`; recovery
#   steps live in docs/configuration/hints.md.
